---
id: UR-002
type: rule
family: unsafe-rendering
title: document.write() / document.writeln() call
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 2

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs]
allowlist:
  [
    '**/*.test.ts',
    '**/*.test.tsx',
    '**/*.test.js',
    '**/*.test.jsx',
    '**/*.spec.ts',
    '**/*.spec.tsx',
    '**/*.spec.js',
    '**/*.spec.jsx',
    '**/__tests__/**',
    '**/tests/**',
    '**/explain/**',
  ]

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: 'document\.write(?:ln)?\s*\('

related: [UR-001, UR-003]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

You're calling `document.write()`. The argument is parsed as HTML, so a
dynamic value carries the same DOM-XSS surface as `innerHTML` (CWE-79) —
and `document.write` after page load rewrites the whole document and
blocks the parser besides.

Build the DOM directly instead: `document.createElement` + `append`, or
assign `el.textContent` for text. If you must insert HTML from dynamic
input, sanitise it with DOMPurify first and write it into a container's
sanitised `innerHTML` rather than through `document.write`.

If the argument is a static constant (e.g. a build-time bootstrap
snippet), suppress UR-002 with a reason noting the input is not dynamic.
